/// A module that names a leaf two other modules declare, with nothing in scope
/// to name either.  Both signatures must be rejected.
///
/// There is no `import` here, deliberately.  `Widget` is declared by
/// `PluralLeafGate::Alpha` and by `PluralLeafGate::Omega`, neither of which
/// this module imports, so under §5.1 the bare `Widget` names no type.
///
/// Both arms are present because sema binds them through different functions:
/// the static template through `find_static_method_template`, the free function
/// through `check_generic_free_call`.  A fix that reached only one would leave
/// the other binding by registration order.
namespace PluralLeafGate::Orphan;

type struct Packer {
    /// Static generic method returning a type this module cannot see.
    static pack<T>(v: T) -> Widget<T> {
        return Widget::<T> { v: v };
    }
}

/// Free function returning a type this module cannot see.
function box_up<T>(v: T) -> Widget<T> {
    return Widget::<T> { v: v };
}
